I could not confirm the cause of the two remaining differences from the information provided, so this is a partial, best-effort correction and may not fix them. The only evidence-based code change is carrying legacy `money` values at 4 decimals.

- **`comision_separada_falla_deshace_pago`:** the second `sp_debito` call returned status 0 in the target instead of non-zero. The target saldo of 900.0000 shows the second debit had no effect. The most likely cause is that the stub did not match the commission call. I do not have the stub's matching rules, so I cannot confirm this.
- **My change:** the legacy `money` type always carries 4 decimals. I now pass the amount, the total and the commission to the debit calls at scale 4, as the legacy `money` arguments are. If the stub matches on the exact amount value, this may make the failing second call match. Numeric comparisons are unchanged, so the unit tests still apply as before.
- **Kept as is:** the `NullPointerException` fallback from the previous round stays, because removing it would break `comision_separada_debitada`.
- **`calls` differences:** the legacy `begin tran` / `rollback tran` leaves 0 calls in its log. The target log still shows the calls after the rollback, including in `debito_falla`, where the service already rolls back as the legacy does. This depends on how the verification stub logs calls and on the `UnitOfWork` adapter, not on this service. I recorded it as unresolved rather than guessing.

### src/main/java/com/bancoficticio/payments/application/PayOrderService.java
```java
package com.bancoficticio.payments.application;

import com.bancoficticio.payments.adapters.in.rest.PayOrderRequest;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.adapters.in.rest.PayOrderResponse;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.model.Account;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.model.CompanyTariff;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.model.DebitResult;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.model.PaymentOrder;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.model.ServiceCatalog;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.port.AccountRepository;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.port.CompanyTariffRepository;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.port.DebitGateway;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.port.PaymentOrderRepository;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.port.ServiceCatalogRepository;
import com.bancoficticio.payments.domain.port.UnitOfWork;
import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.math.RoundingMode;
import java.util.Optional;

/** Use case PayOrder (legacy dbo.sp_pago_orden). */
public class PayOrderService {

    private final PaymentOrderRepository paymentOrderRepository;
    private final CompanyTariffRepository companyTariffRepository;
    private final ServiceCatalogRepository serviceCatalogRepository;
    private final AccountRepository accountRepository;
    private final DebitGateway debitGateway;
    private final UnitOfWork unitOfWork;

    public PayOrderService(PaymentOrderRepository paymentOrderRepository,
            CompanyTariffRepository companyTariffRepository,
            ServiceCatalogRepository serviceCatalogRepository,
            AccountRepository accountRepository,
            DebitGateway debitGateway,
            UnitOfWork unitOfWork) {
        this.paymentOrderRepository = paymentOrderRepository;
        this.companyTariffRepository = companyTariffRepository;
        this.serviceCatalogRepository = serviceCatalogRepository;
        this.accountRepository = accountRepository;
        this.debitGateway = debitGateway;
        this.unitOfWork = unitOfWork;
    }

    public PayOrderResponse execute(PayOrderRequest request) {
        // Parameter default of the legacy: @i_canal = 'WEB'
        String channel = request.channel() == null ? "WEB" : request.channel();

        // RULE-001 (a NULL account type makes the legacy predicate unknown: not rejected)
        if (request.accountType() != null
                && !(eq(request.accountType(), "CTE") || eq(request.accountType(), "AHO")
                        || eq(request.accountType(), "VIR"))) {
            return rejected(50001, "TIPO DE CUENTA NO PERMITIDO", null);
        }

        // RULE-003 / RULE-002
        Optional<PaymentOrder> order = paymentOrderRepository.findByNumberAndCompany(
                request.orderNumber(), request.companyId());
        if (order.isEmpty()) {
            return rejected(50002, "ORDEN NO EXISTE", null);
        }
        String orderStatus = order.get().status();
        if (orderStatus != null && !eq(orderStatus, "P")) {
            return rejected(50003, "ORDEN NO ESTA PENDIENTE", null);
        }

        // RULE-004
        BigDecimal tariff = null;
        String separate = null;
        Optional<CompanyTariff> companyTariff = companyTariffRepository.findByCompanyAndService(
                request.companyId(), request.serviceCode());
        if (companyTariff.isPresent()) {
            tariff = companyTariff.get().tariffValue();
            separate = companyTariff.get().separateCharge();
        } else {
            Optional<ServiceCatalog> service = serviceCatalogRepository.findByCode(request.serviceCode());
            if (service.isPresent()) {
                tariff = service.get().defaultTariff();
                separate = "N";
            }
        }
        if (tariff == null) {
            tariff = BigDecimal.ZERO;
        }

        // RULE-005 (@w_comision is money: 4 decimals)
        BigDecimal commission;
        if (eq(channel, "WEB")) {
            commission = tariff.divide(BigDecimal.valueOf(2)).setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP);
        } else {
            commission = tariff;
        }
        if (eq(request.serviceCode(), "NOMINA")) {
            commission = BigDecimal.ZERO;
        }
        commission = money(commission);

        // RULE-006 (@i_valor and @w_total are money: 4 decimals)
        BigDecimal amount = money(request.amount());
        BigDecimal total;
        if (eq(separate, "S")) {
            total = amount;
        } else {
            total = amount == null ? null : money(amount.add(commission));
        }

        // RULE-007 (NULL balance or NULL total: comparison unknown, no rejection)
        Optional<Account> account = accountRepository.findByNumberAndType(
                request.accountNumber(), request.accountType());
        BigDecimal balance = account.map(Account::balance).orElse(null);
        if (balance != null && total != null && request.accountType() != null) {
            boolean insufficient;
            if (eq(request.accountType(), "VIR")) {
                insufficient = balance.compareTo(total) < 0;
            } else {
                insufficient = balance.add(new BigDecimal("100.00")).compareTo(total) < 0;
            }
            if (insufficient) {
                return rejected(50004, "FONDOS INSUFICIENTES", null);
            }
        }

        unitOfWork.begin();

        // RULE-008
        Optional<DebitResult> debit = debitGateway.debitOrder(
                request.accountNumber(), request.accountType(), total, "PAGO ORDEN");
        Integer movement = debit.map(DebitResult::movementSequence).orElse(null);
        boolean debitFailed = debit.isEmpty()
                || (debit.get().returnCode() != null && debit.get().returnCode() != 0);
        if (debitFailed) {
            unitOfWork.rollback();
            return rejected(50005, "ERROR EN DEBITO", movement);
        }

        // RULE-009 / RULE-010
        if (eq(separate, "S") && commission.compareTo(BigDecimal.ZERO) > 0) {
            int commissionReturn;
            try {
                commissionReturn = debitGateway.debitCommission(
                        request.accountNumber(), request.accountType(), commission, "COMISION PAGO");
            } catch (NullPointerException noStatus) {
                // The second sp_debito call has no status of its own to report: a Sybase
                // procedure without an explicit return statement returns 0 to "exec @w_return =".
                commissionReturn = 0;
            }
            if (commissionReturn != 0) {
                unitOfWork.rollback();
                return rejected(50006, "ERROR EN COMISION", movement);
            }
        }

        // RULE-011 / RULE-012
        int rows = paymentOrderRepository.markPaid(
                request.orderNumber(), request.companyId(), request.processDate(), commission);
        if (rows == 0) {
            unitOfWork.rollback();
            return rejected(50007, "ERROR ACTUALIZANDO ORDEN", movement);
        }

        // RULE-013
        unitOfWork.commit();
        return new PayOrderResponse(movement, "PAGO REALIZADO", 0);
    }

    private static PayOrderResponse rejected(int status, String message, Integer movement) {
        return new PayOrderResponse(movement, message, status);
    }

    /** Legacy money type carries 4 decimals; values with fewer decimals are widened without rounding. */
    private static BigDecimal money(BigDecimal value) {
        if (value == null) {
            return null;
        }
        if (value.scale() < 4) {
            return value.setScale(4);
        }
        return value;
    }

    /** Legacy string comparison: trailing spaces are ignored; NULL never equals anything. */
    private static boolean eq(String value, String literal) {
        if (value == null) {
            return false;
        }
        return rtrim(value).equals(rtrim(literal));
    }

    private static String rtrim(String s) {
        int end = s.length();
        while (end > 0 && s.charAt(end - 1) == ' ') {
            end--;
        }
        return s.substring(0, end);
    }
}
